== Review of section 0 (by hand, 8 Nov)
The five calls in loop conditions are all in B0-B2 testbench code, written before D41:
  tb_pkg.sv:73 r.len() and tb_router.sv:596 sb_tsend.exists() are built-in methods;
  run_ctrl.sv:58 sb_pkg::outstanding() and tests_func.svh:302 waits() contain no loop;
  tb_router.sv:475 all_idle() has loops but sits in a while condition, and R01-R04 give
  identical counts on Verilator, xsim and Riviera-PRO.
The hang D41 guards against came from a call in a for condition (U05). No change: B0-B2
are closed and verified, and the B3 code has no such call.
Section 4's MULTITOP lines are one warning (three lines), as in B2: the design pane's
modules a test does not use are extra tops (README Section 3); the testbench pane adds
only the chosen test's top.
